  The only things required in the game are survival and getting the
amulet of Yendor to an appropriate altar on the Astral Plane.  Use
anything and everything to achieve those.  Nothing else is required.
That doesn't mean everything else is gravy.

  One player ascended using a box as wielded weapon for the whole game.
Does that make a wielded weapon "gravy?"  Players have also ascended
foodless.  Does that mean it's a good idea?  Playing illiterate means
doing without Elbereth.  (Well, sort of.  A scroll of scare monster
still works on the ground and doesn't break illiterate conduct.)  Does
it make the game harder?  You betcha.

  I've ascended wishless.  So wishes obviously aren't necessary to
ascend.  Do I recommend that to someone asking for help?  No.

  Elbereth is not an instawin.  It's not even a guaranteed win.  I found
out the hard way that unlimited 100% guaranteed Elbereths still let you
be killed by ranged attacks.  That doesn't even count all the monsters
that ignore Elbereth.  (All you posters that claim Elbereth is "too
powerful?"  I want my money back!)  What Elbereth can do is let players
live long enough to start learning the game.

  No one thing is critical.  Ascending in Nethack means using a lot of
things, usual as many as possible.  Anyone who watches mrivan's
ascension ttyrecs on NAO will see him use anything and everything.
Usually you won't recognize half of what he's doing.  (I once spent half
an hour researching a ttyrec to see how he'd managed to accomplish
something.)

  So use it all until you get your first ascension.  Keep ascending
until you're bored, then start doing conducts.  (Recommending conducts
to someone asking for help in surviving....)


